NoCable Launcher for Linux

Linux port maintained by Tyler-Vibe.
Based on the approach and cable signature documented in Maxx53/NoCableLauncher:
https://github.com/Maxx53/NoCableLauncher (GPL-2.0).
Historical multiplayer inspiration: phobos2077's AutoIt nocable script.

The public PSARC format constants are used for archive interoperability.
The game, Proton, GTK, PipeWire, Python libraries, and archive utilities are
separate dependencies with their own licenses; their binaries are not included.

This source distribution is provided under GNU GPL version 2 (see LICENSE).
It includes no Ubisoft game assets and is not endorsed by Ubisoft.
